WHY

`player_seasons.csv` is derived from the squad statistics tables of English
Wikipedia's Premier League club-season articles. Wikipedia's text is licensed
CC BY-SA 4.0, and an adapted database built from it carries the same terms.


ATTRIBUTION

The material is the squad statistics tables of the 100 English Wikipedia
club-season articles covering the twenty Premier League clubs of each season from
2021-22 to 2025-26. Attribution to a Wikipedia article's authors is given by
linking the article, whose page history is its author list.

`sources.json` lists all 100 individually — title, URL, and the revision id each
article's figures were read from — which is the resource this notice points at.

Changes made: the per-competition appearance and goal figures were extracted from
each article's squad statistics tables; the Premier League columns were kept and
the cup and European ones discarded; players with no Premier League appearance
were left out; and the result was reshaped into one row per player per season per
club, keyed by the player's Wikipedia page title.


IF YOU REDISTRIBUTE THIS FILE

Modified or not, it stays under CC BY-SA 4.0, and this notice and `sources.json`
should travel with it. Nothing here restricts what you may do with the code.
